# TypeScript migration

`src/` implementation files are **TypeScript only**. New JS/JSX under `src/` is forbidden.
`@ts-nocheck`, `@ts-expect-error`, and `@ts-ignore` are **forbidden** (count must stay **0**).

## Policy

1. **New files under `src/`** — `.ts` / `.tsx` only. Never add `.js` / `.jsx` in `src/`.
2. **Directive suppressions** — do not add. Prefer real types, `src/types/*.d.ts` augmentation, or a narrow boundary cast (see `ts-expect-error-cleanup` rule).
3. **`allowJs: true`** — kept for non-`src` / tooling edge cases; `checkJs` stays off. Do not use `allowJs` as a reason to grow JS in `src/`.
4. **When editing** — improve types at the touch point when cheap; do not reintroduce nocheck/expect-error or JS.
5. Prefer **English** in new code comments if Korean Unicode might corrupt.

## Out of scope (separate tracks)

- Turning on project-wide `checkJs`

## Examples

```text
❌ BAD — add src/features/foo.js or restore @ts-nocheck / @ts-expect-error
❌ BAD — new .jsx "just for now" under src/components
✅ GOOD — new helper as .ts / .tsx
✅ GOOD — vendor gaps via src/types/*.d.ts or narrow cast
✅ GOOD — eslint ban-ts-comment blocks nocheck and expect-error project-wide
```
